# NOTE (2026-08-11): / and /index.html deliberately KEEP the platform default
# (max-age=0, must-revalidate) rather than no-store. A no-store HTML was tried and correlated
# with blank-white cold loads on weak cellular: every navigation had to complete a network fetch
# before anything rendered, and a slow response is not a fetch failure, so the service worker's
# cached-shell fallback never engaged. The revalidating default keeps deploys fresh via ETag.

# The service worker and its asset manifest carry stable names, so they must never be edge- or
# browser-cached: a stale copy pins an installed PWA to old assets across deploys. no-store forces
# every update-check to fetch the freshly-deployed, build-id-stamped copy (see generate-sw-assets.mjs).
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-store, must-revalidate
/sw-assets.json
  Cache-Control: no-store, must-revalidate
